<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chamorro people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as CHamoru</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chamorro are the indigenous people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariana-islands">Mariana Islands</a>, including Guam, whose ancestors settled the islands about 3,500 years ago. They built latte stone house foundations and lived by fishing and farming. Spanish colonisation from 1668, war and disease reduced their numbers sharply, but the Chamorro language and culture survive, and they form the largest ethnic group on Guam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chamorro-people.jpg" alt="Chamorro people" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marilyn Sourgose · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chamorro_performers_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
